course: dictionary
lesson: 3347
title: Exam: a test and a check
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An exam is a test to see how much you know. «Growing up brings big choices: how to look after money, what work to do, which exams and courses to take» shows that exams are part of school and college life. When you meet exam, ask what it is for: is it a test of learning, or a check of your body?
explain: Exam is short for examination. The words around it give clues. «Exams like GCSEs and A levels open doors later» is about school tests, and words like revise, pass and results tell you the same thing. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Exams like GCSEs and A levels open doors later" still makes sense with "tests like GCSEs and A levels".
explain: The word also has a health sense. An eye exam is a check by a doctor or dentist, so it looks at your eyes or teeth, not at what you have learned. Read the clues each time: if the sentence is about school, marks or passing, it means a test.
fact: An exam is a test at school or college to see how much you know.
fact: An exam can also be a check by a doctor or dentist, like an eye exam.
fact: Exam is short for examination.
fact: You can take or sit an exam, pass an exam, and look at exam results and an exam paper.
fact: «Kǎoshì» means a test or exam in Chinese, and «kǎo de zěnmeyàng?» means how did the test go?
exercise: «Growing up brings big choices: which exams and courses to take.» What does exams mean here? | Trips to the seaside | *Tests to show how much you know | Hot dinners | Bags for shopping
exercise: Mia has an eye exam at the hospital. What is an eye exam? | A game played in class | A painting of an eye | *A check of your eyes by a doctor | A race to see who blinks first
exercise: «Exams like GCSEs and A levels open doors later, but people who do badly can retake them.» What does retake mean? | Read the book twice | *Take the test again | Go on holiday | Give up for ever
test: What does «kǎoshì» mean? | *A test or exam | A train ticket | A bowl of rice
test: In a school, what is an exam paper? | A form for a bank | A letter to a friend | A newspaper article | *The questions and marks for a test
exam: Exam is short for which longer word? | Excitement | Exit | Example | *Examination
</br>
